 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 534311,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "To make a trim for the window in the figure shown, you need the perimeter. How many feet of trim do you need to buy?\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/dffffd07d8055c4c.png\" alt=\"A polygon shows a semicircle resting on top of a rectangle. The length and width of the rectangle measure 5.3 and 2. The radius of the semicircle measures 2.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The trim will cover 2 feet along the bottom as well as the 5.3-foot sides, plus the semicircle at the top. The semicircle has a diameter of 2 feet.</p>\n<p>The circumference of a circle with diameter <i>d</i> is <span data-math=\"C = \\pi d\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The distance around the semicircle would be half of that.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\rm{semicircle}} = \\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\left( {2{\\rm{\\ feet}}} \\right) \\approx 3.14{\\rm{\\ ft}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The total trim needed: <span data-math=\"2 {\\rm\\ ft} + (5.3\\ {\\rm\\ ft})(2) + 3.14{\\rm\\ ft} = 15.74{\\rm\\ ft}\"></span></p>\n<p>You need 15.74 feet of trim.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "You need to buy 15.74 feet of trim."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
